    "text": "The dilution processes of different aqueous solutions with water are given in LIST-I. The effects of dilution of the solutions on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></math> are given in LIST-II.<br />(Note: The degree of dissociation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></mfenced></math> of&nbsp;a weak acid and a weak base is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>;</mo></math>&nbsp;the degree of hydrolysis of salt is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>[</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></math> represents the concentration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math> ions)<table border=\"1\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>LIST &ndash;I</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: justify;\">LIST -II</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>A)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>mL</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>of</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>NaOH</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>mL</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>of</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>.1</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math>acetic acid&nbsp;diluted to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>mL</mi></math>.</td>\t\t\t<td>P)</td>\t\t\t<td>The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></math> does not change on dilution.</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>B)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>mL</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>of</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>NaOH</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>mL</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> acetic acid diluted to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>mL</mi></math>.</td>\t\t\t<td>Q)</td>\t\t\t<td>The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mtext>[H</mtext><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></math> changes to half of its initial value on dilution.</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>C)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>mL</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>of</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>.1</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>HCl</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>mL</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.1</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math>ammonia solution&nbsp;diluted to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>mL</mi></math>.</td>\t\t\t<td>R)</td>\t\t\t<td>The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></math> changes to two times&nbsp;its initial value on dilution.</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>D)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>mL</mi></math> saturated solution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ni</mi><msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math> in equilibrium with excess of solid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ni</mi><msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is diluted to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math>&nbsp;(solid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ni</mi><msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is still present after dilution).</td>\t\t\t<td>S)</td>\t\t\t<td>The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></math> changes to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt></msqrt></math> times its initial value on dilution.</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>T)</td>\t\t\t<td>The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></math> changes to <math><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math> times&nbsp;its initial value on dilution.</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><br />Match each process given in LIST-I with one or more effect(s) in LIST-II. The correct option is"
